--- META ---
name: CreateTask picks the stub by priority value
summary: high and normal are served by their own stubs, not by the critical one that carries the effect
tags: [priority]

--- ENDPOINT ---
tasktracker.TaskService/CreateTask

--- REQUEST ---
{
  "assignee": "dev2",
  "priority": "high",
  "title": "Investigate flaky test"
}

--- RESPONSE ---
{
  "task_id": "high-created",
  "ok": true
}
// The same method with another priority must fall to the other stub

--- ENDPOINT ---
tasktracker.TaskService/CreateTask

--- REQUEST ---
{
  "assignee": "dev3",
  "priority": "normal",
  "title": "Update changelog"
}

--- RESPONSE ---
{
  "task_id": "normal-created",
  "ok": true
}
